{
  "$comment": [
    "DK-11: one set of mcp.json cases run by the three readers of the file, so they cannot drift: the daemon (packages/daemon/src/connections/config.ts), the shell (apps/desktop/src-tauri/src/connections/document.rs) and the app's form (apps/desktop/src/connections/validation.ts).",
    "documents: run by the daemon and the shell, which read whole files. `at` is where the shell says the file is wrong (shown in the connections screen); `daemonAt` is every path the daemon logs. Known difference: the daemon names the server, the shell the key inside it, since zod reports a failed union at the server; and the shell names only the first wrong place.",
    "serverNames and urls: run by all three; the daemon and the shell read each inside a one-server document, the app's form checks the field itself.",
    "expectedDifferences: a case on which one reader is known to disagree, as { validator: daemon | shell | app, list: documents | serverNames | urls, case: its name or value, valid: what that reader says, comment: why it is left so }; that reader is held to its own verdict. Empty while the three agree."
  ],
  "documents": [
    {
      "name": "no server",
      "document": {
        "mcpServers": {}
      },
      "valid": true
    },
    {
      "name": "a process server with every field",
      "document": {
        "mcpServers": {
          "zeta": {
            "command": "npx",
            "args": ["-y", "zeta-mcp", ""],
            "env": {
              "TOKEN": "@keychain",
              "EMPTY": ""
            },
            "readOnly": ["search"]
          }
        }
      },
      "valid": true
    },
    {
      "name": "an HTTPS server with every field",
      "document": {
        "mcpServers": {
          "alpha": {
            "url": "https://example.com/mcp",
            "headers": {
              "Authorization": "Bearer b-2"
            },
            "readOnly": ["list"]
          }
        }
      },
      "valid": true
    },
    {
      "name": "plain HTTP to this machine",
      "document": {
        "mcpServers": {
          "local": {
            "url": "http://127.0.0.1:8080/mcp"
          }
        }
      },
      "valid": true
    },
    {
      "name": "several servers, each of its kind",
      "document": {
        "mcpServers": {
          "zeta": {
            "command": "zeta-mcp"
          },
          "alpha": {
            "url": "https://example.com/mcp"
          },
          "My notes 2.0": {
            "command": "notes"
          }
        }
      },
      "valid": true
    },
    {
      "name": "a top level that is a list",
      "document": [],
      "valid": false,
      "at": "its top level",
      "daemonAt": [""]
    },
    {
      "name": "a top level that is null",
      "document": null,
      "valid": false,
      "at": "its top level",
      "daemonAt": [""]
    },
    {
      "name": "a top-level key besides mcpServers",
      "document": {
        "mcpServers": {},
        "version": 1
      },
      "valid": false,
      "at": "version",
      "daemonAt": [""]
    },
    {
      "name": "no mcpServers",
      "document": {},
      "valid": false,
      "at": "mcpServers",
      "daemonAt": ["mcpServers"]
    },
    {
      "name": "mcpServers as a list",
      "document": {
        "mcpServers": []
      },
      "valid": false,
      "at": "mcpServers",
      "daemonAt": ["mcpServers"]
    },
    {
      "name": "a server that is a text",
      "document": {
        "mcpServers": {
          "off": "disabled for now"
        }
      },
      "valid": false,
      "at": "mcpServers.off",
      "daemonAt": ["mcpServers.off"]
    },
    {
      "name": "a server that is null",
      "document": {
        "mcpServers": {
          "zeta": null
        }
      },
      "valid": false,
      "at": "mcpServers.zeta",
      "daemonAt": ["mcpServers.zeta"]
    },
    {
      "name": "a server name the daemon refuses",
      "document": {
        "mcpServers": {
          "a/b": {
            "command": "x"
          }
        }
      },
      "valid": false,
      "at": "mcpServers.a/b",
      "daemonAt": ["mcpServers.a/b"]
    },
    {
      "name": "a key other MCP clients write (type)",
      "document": {
        "mcpServers": {
          "zeta": {
            "command": "npx",
            "type": "stdio"
          }
        }
      },
      "valid": false,
